@startuml USER-FLOWS-sla
' Customer Support CRM — user flows. READ-ONLY DOCUMENTATION, nothing here is invented.
' Drawn from the repository at commit 969bb31 (2026-09-01): the Angular routes and guards,
' the ASP.NET Core controllers and their authorization policies, the Application services,
' the EF Core entities and migrations, and the approved documents under docs/ and .squad/.
' Red text marks what is NOT IMPLEMENTED. Index of all 11 diagrams: docs/USER-FLOWS.md
' Diagram 8 of 11 — SLA monitoring, escalation and notifications
title SLA monitoring, escalation and notifications\nThe flow that does not start in the browser (AD-6, A-3, A-13, A-21)

skinparam shadowing false
|#FFF4E5|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
|#FFE9D6|Application services|
|#FDEAF1|SQL Server|
|#E8F0FE|Staff browser|

|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
start
:Host starts → one sweep immediately, then every\nSweepIntervalSeconds (PeriodicTimer).\nNo queue, no broker, no external scheduler;
repeat
  :Create a DI scope; set the SYSTEM identity;
  |Application services|
  :SlaEvaluationService.EvaluateDueTicketsAsync;
  |SQL Server|
  :SELECT Tickets WHERE the status is not terminal AND\n( (FirstResponseDueAt <= now AND NOT FirstResponseBreached\n    AND FirstRespondedAt IS NULL)\n  OR (ResolutionDueAt <= now AND NOT ResolutionBreached\n    AND ResolvedAt IS NULL) )\n— served by the two filtered indexes;
  if (any tickets due ?) then (yes)
    |Application services|
    :Latch the breach flag(s) — idempotent by construction:\nthe flags this pass sets are in the next pass's predicate;
    :Escalate through TicketLifecycleService.EscalateAsync\n(actor = System) — the SAME path the manual button uses,\nnot a second implementation;
    :Resolve recipients via IEscalationRecipientPolicy (A-21):\nthe department's manager, else all Managers,\nelse all Administrators;
    |SQL Server|
    :UPDATE Tickets (breach flags, priority +1)\nINSERT TicketActivity(Escalated)\nINSERT AuditEntry(TicketEscalated)\nINSERT Notification(SlaBreached, TicketEscalated)\nCOMMITTED ONCE for the whole sweep;
  else (no)
    |Application services|
    :Nothing to do;
  endif
repeat while (host running ?) is (yes) not (shutdown)
|SlaMonitorHostedService (in-process timer)|
:A failed tick is logged and the loop continues;
stop

|Staff browser|
partition "How a notification reaches a person" {
  :Every navigation calls NotificationStore.refresh()\n— staff only, skipped for a Customer session;
  :GET /notifications?pageSize=10 → bell badge and panel;
  :Opening one marks it read:\nPOST /notifications/{id}/read (204, idempotent).\nNo optimistic decrement (UI-8); no mark-all-read (AP-18);
  :The full list is at /workspace/notifications;
}

note right
  **The four notification types (A-13), and no others**
  · TicketAssigned  — manual assignment, or round-robin
  · SlaBreached     — raised by the sweep, the only system actor
  · TicketEscalated — manual escalate, or the sweep
  · CustomerReplied — a customer posted on the portal

  **Known simplification, reported not fixed (A-3, PF-5):**
  the clock is 24/7 wall-clock from createdAt — no business hours,
  no holidays, and Pending does NOT pause it. A ticket resolved
  without an outbound reply stays first-response breached.

  **NOT IMPLEMENTED:** e-mail, SMS or push delivery. A notification
  is a database row read by the in-app bell — nothing else.
end note
@enduml
